Knowledge stops being something one person owns. It becomes something the whole company owns. When an expert shares a skill, that knowledge stays with PNC forever. It does not go on vacation. It does not leave the company. It just keeps helping people, day after day.

For developers, this means less time stuck and more time building. Less time searching for answers and more time solving real problems. New team members get up to speed faster. Every team writes better, more consistent code.

And for the bank, it means we move faster, we build with higher quality, and we free our people to focus on the work that matters most — solving hard business problems for our customers.

